  "summary": "One sad MS Paint face, ten thousand moods: the internet's emotional alphabet.",
  "description": "Wojak (\"feels guy\", originated Krautchan 2010) became the internet's emotional shorthand: a bald line-drawn figure whose variants map entire worldviews — doomer (black hoodie, existential dread), bloomers (post-doomer hope), coomer, NPC (grey conformism), soyjak (excitable mockery), tradwife, zoomer — each a ready-made character for forum psychodrama. The doomer-verse extended into full comic genres (doomer girl romance arcs) and the \"wojak compass\" template where memes self-organize into ideological charts. As visual culture: a folk character system as expressive as theater masks, constantly recombined, occasionally poisoned by its political uses, and never done spawning variants.",
  "culturalContext": "Wojak became the internet's emotional alphabet: feels guy's variants (doomer, bloomer, NPC, soyjak) map entire worldviews as reusable characters, the doomer-verse spawned full comic genres, and the face system now functions as folk theater masks for online psychodrama.",
